# Pairs with BootstrapHandoffLosesNothing. Reproduces production before #4604:
# the snapshot drain discards the ApplyResult, so a row the replication
# applier defers - the coordinated-restore receive fence (#1173), an in-flight
# duplicate (#4465), a restored copy's fence (#4593) - is neither applied nor
# re-drained, yet the drain completes and the handoff pins the frontier past
# it. A source write that reaches the target only through the snapshot, because
# the stream resumes beyond it, is then neither absorbed nor on its way.
MODULE: BootstrapHandoffLosesNothingDrainDropsDeferred
TARGET: BootstrapHandoffLosesNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the drain completes past rows the applier deferred, so a source write carried only by the snapshot is lost
PERTURBS: Bootstrap

--- FIND
    /\ val' = [val EXCEPT ![BootTarget] = [k \in Keys |-> @[k] \cup val[BootSource][k]]]
    /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![BootTarget] =
                    @ \cup {<<BootSource, k, Ver(BootSource, k)>> : k \in {j \in Keys : val[BootSource][j] # {}}}]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the applier defers some rows and the drain completes past them
\* (LatticeBootstrapCoordinatorGrain ignored ApplyResult.Deferred), applying
\* and seeding nothing for a deferred row.
    /\ \E deferred \in SUBSET Keys :
          /\ val' = [val EXCEPT ![BootTarget] =
                        [k \in Keys |-> @[k] \cup (IF k \in deferred THEN {} ELSE val[BootSource][k])]]
          /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![BootTarget] =
                          @ \cup {<<BootSource, k, Ver(BootSource, k)>> : k \in {j \in Keys \ deferred : val[BootSource][j] # {}}}]
--- END